# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled test binaries inside the test trees.
#
# This used to be a hand-maintained list of individual NAMES — the same
# deny-list shape this project keeps replacing with gates. Every new test that
# compiles to a binary had to be added by hand, and any that wasn't got
# committed. It failed exactly that way: measured 2026-08-23, **560 ELF
# binaries (11 MB) were tracked**, they re-dirty `git status` after every test
# run, and they had been arriving one commit at a time since 43126a1.
#
# The durable rule: every test SOURCE in these trees carries an extension, so an
# extension-less file in them is a compiled artifact BY CONSTRUCTION (verified:
# of every extension-less tracked file in these directories, all 558 were ELF).
# Ignore those, re-include anything with a dot, and re-ignore the build
# extensions at the end of this file so the `*.*` negations cannot resurrect
# them. A new test binary can no longer be committed by omission.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rust_tests/*
!rust_tests/*.*
!rust_tests/*/
zig_tests/*
!zig_tests/*.*
!zig_tests/*/
test_modules/*
!test_modules/*.*
!test_modules/*/
tests/zer/*
!tests/zer/*.*
!tests/zer/*/
tests/zer_fail/*
!tests/zer_fail/*.*
!tests/zer_fail/*/
tests/zer_proof/*
!tests/zer_proof/*.*
!tests/zer_proof/*/
tests/zer_trap/*
!tests/zer_trap/*.*
!tests/zer_trap/*/
tests/zer_gaps/*
!tests/zer_gaps/*.*
!tests/zer_gaps/*/
examples/cve-demos/*
!examples/cve-demos/*.*
!examples/cve-demos/*/

# Re-ignore build artifacts LAST: the `!<dir>/*.*` negations above would
# otherwise override the `*.o` / `*.exe` rules at the top of this file for any
# path inside a test tree.
*.o
*.exe
